# File: tests/blender/test_rig_*.py (scenarios map 1:1 to tests)
# Generated from: specs/32-support-humanoid-rigging-and-animation-import/requirements.md
Feature: Humanoid rigging and animation import

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Humanoid rigging uses local Blender tooling
    Given a T-pose "Hero" humanoid mesh and landmarks for it
    And outbound network connections are blocked
    When rig_humanoid runs with body type "humanoid"
    Then it returns status "ok"
    And SK_Hero has exactly the 26 UE5 Mannequin deform bones in the Mannequin hierarchy
    And SM_Hero is parented to SK_Hero with every vertex weighted
    And no network connection was attempted and Rigify was not enabled

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Rigging again replaces the rig
    Given a rigged "Hero"
    When rig_humanoid runs again
    Then exactly one SK_Hero exists with the same bones

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Library clips are retargeted and exported with provenance
    Given a rigged "Hero" and a library with an FBX "Idle" and a BVH "Walk" on a Mixamo skeleton
    When import_animations runs and export_rigged writes to an output folder
    Then SM_Hero.fbx re-imported in a fresh Blender has the 26 Mannequin bones and "Idle" and "Walk" actions with their frame ranges
    And thigh_l follows LeftUpLeg within 1 degree at a sampled frame
    And nmg-animations.json records each clip's frame range, fps, library, source file, SHA-256, and source skeleton

  @SCN004
  Scenario Outline: Unsupported requests fail honestly
    Given <request>
    When the matching rig_core function runs
    Then it returns status "<status>" with code "<code>", a message, and a remediation
    And no network connection was attempted

    Examples:
      | request                                   | status                   | code                         |
      | a "quadruped" body type                   | follow-up spike required | rig.unsupported_body         |
      | asymmetric humanoid landmarks             | fallback required        | rig.unclear_humanoid         |
      | a humanoid with arms raised overhead      | fallback required        | rig.pose_not_neutral         |
      | a text-driven motion prompt               | follow-up spike required | anim.text_motion_unsupported |
      | a clip name missing from the library      | fallback required        | anim.clip_not_found          |

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Operators share the implementation
    Given the add-on is enabled
    When each rigging operator runs with the same inputs as a direct rig_core call
    Then scene.nmg_game_dev.last_result equals the direct call's result
    And the operator returns FINISHED for "ok" and CANCELLED otherwise
